{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>For stolen I was stolen from the land of the Hebrews.</b> Because Joseph made known that he was a Hebrew, he therefore merited to be buried in his land. But Moses our teacher, about whom it is said ״an Egyptian man saved us,״ which implies that he did not disclose to them the land of his birth, did not merit to be buried in his land."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:06.908736120Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}